  "sections": {
    "work": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "[La Tour de l'Horloge] was drawn and etched in 1852 while alterations were in progress which materially altered the appearance of Le Chatelet. This plate has always struck me as being a very straightforward and masterly portrait of a building, but without so much personal expression as Meryon generally contrived to impart to his other etchings.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Campbell Dodgson",
          "title": "The Etchings of Charles Meryon",
          "publisher": "The Studio (Internet Archive scan)",
          "year": "1921",
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft",
          "readAt": "https://archive.org/stream/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft/etchingsofcharle00dodguoft_djvu.txt",
          "tier": 2,
          "accessed": "2026-11-26",
          "page": "14"
        }
      }
    ],
    "moment": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Louis Napoleon and Baron Haussmann destroyed picturesque Paris to the consternation of Meryon, who to the eye of an archaeologist united the soul of an artist. He loved old Paris.",
        "source": {
          "author": "James Huneker",
          "title": "Promenades of an Impressionist",
          "publisher": "T. Werner Laurie (Internet Archive scan)",
          "year": "1910",
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/promenadesofimpr00huneuoft",
          "readAt": "https://archive.org/stream/promenadesofimpr00huneuoft/promenadesofimpr00huneuoft_djvu.txt",
          "tier": 3,
          "accessed": "2026-11-26",
          "page": "180"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "In more than one case, for instance, he hurried with particular affection to etch his impression of some old-world building which was on the point of destruction, as Napoleon III tore down buildings to reconstruct Paris with wide boulevards.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "Charles Meryon",
          "publisher": "Wikipedia",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Meryon",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
          "accessed": "2026-11-26"
        }
      }
    ],
    "matters": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Forty years ago Meryon would gladly have sold one of his finest prints for the price of his breakfast.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Frederick Keppel",
          "title": "Charles Meryon: A Biographical Sketch",
          "publisher": "Frederick Keppel & Co. (Internet Archive scan)",
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/charlesmeryonbio00kepp",
          "readAt": "https://archive.org/stream/charlesmeryonbio00kepp/charlesmeryonbio00kepp_djvu.txt",
          "tier": 3,
          "accessed": "2026-11-26"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "A \"Tour de l'Horloge,\" which two or three years after it was first issued sold for half a crown, in May 1903 fetched [£]70.",
        "source": {
